From: Mateusz Krawczuk <mateusz.krawczuk@cybrixsystems.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: stmmac: dwmac-dwc-qos-eth: request interconnect bandwidth on Tegra EQOS

tegra186.dtsi/tegra194.dtsi describe the EQOS DMA memory paths:

  interconnects = <&mc TEGRA..._MEMORY_CLIENT_EQOSR &emc>,
                  <&mc TEGRA..._MEMORY_CLIENT_EQOSW &emc>;
  interconnect-names = "dma-mem", "write";

but no driver ever consumed them, so the memory subsystem never learns
that the NIC is active.  On Tegra194 there is no firmware bandwidth
manager either (MRQ_BWMGR_INT is Tegra234+), so the EMC sits at its
conservative boot frequency and the resulting DMA latency overflows
the EQOS RX FIFO under sustained load: RX overruns, DMA stalls and TX
watchdog resets at default clocks, all "fixed" by jetson_clocks maxing
the EMC.  The same gap exists in NVIDIA's downstream nvethernet driver
(no bwmgr/ICC calls), which is why L4T shows the identical symptom.

Acquire the optional "dma-mem"/"write" ICC paths in the Tegra glue and
request bandwidth at probe.  The average is the 1 GbE line rate; the
peak acts as a memory-frequency floor request, which the (patched)
tegra186-emc provider converts into an EMC clk floor (~625 MHz with
the 10 GBps default) - in the range L4T's bwmgr used for ISO clients.
Both values are module parameters
(dwc_eth_dwmac.eqos_icc_{avg,peak}_kbps=) so the minimal sufficient
floor can be measured empirically.

Device trees without interconnect properties get NULL paths and are
unaffected; a not-yet-probed MC defers the probe as usual.

Upstream-Status: Pending (mainline candidate; upstream would likely
want the request tied to ndo_open/close and the floor policy debated)
Signed-off-by: Mateusz Krawczuk <mateusz.krawczuk@cybrixsystems.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-dwc-qos-eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-dwc-qos-eth.c
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@
 #include <linux/device.h>
 #include <linux/gpio/consumer.h>
 #include <linux/ethtool.h>
+#include <linux/interconnect.h>
 #include <linux/io.h>
 #include <linux/iopoll.h>
 #include <linux/ioport.h>
@@ -33,6 +34,55 @@
 	struct gpio_desc *reset;
 };
 
+/*
+ * Bandwidth requested on the "dma-mem" (read) and "write" interconnect
+ * paths (MC memory clients EQOSR/EQOSW towards the EMC).  The average
+ * is the 1 GbE line rate.  The peak acts as a memory frequency floor
+ * request: on Tegra194 no firmware bandwidth manager exists, so DMA
+ * latency at the BPMP's boot EMC frequency is high enough to overflow
+ * the EQOS RX FIFO and stall the DMA under sustained load.  The default
+ * (10 GBps per direction) maps to an EMC floor of ~625 MHz via the
+ * tegra186-emc provider, matching the range L4T's bwmgr used for ISO
+ * clients.  Tunable for measurement via
+ * dwc_eth_dwmac.eqos_icc_peak_kbps= on the kernel command line.
+ */
+static unsigned int eqos_icc_avg_kbps = 125000;
+module_param(eqos_icc_avg_kbps, uint, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(eqos_icc_avg_kbps, "Average DRAM bandwidth request per direction (kBps)");
+
+static unsigned int eqos_icc_peak_kbps = 10000000;
+module_param(eqos_icc_peak_kbps, uint, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(eqos_icc_peak_kbps, "Peak DRAM bandwidth request per direction (kBps), acts as EMC floor");
+
+static int tegra_eqos_init_icc(struct device *dev)
+{
+	struct icc_path *read, *write;
+	int err;
+
+	/* Optional: absent from pre-interconnect device trees */
+	read = devm_of_icc_get(dev, "dma-mem");
+	if (IS_ERR(read))
+		return PTR_ERR(read);
+
+	write = devm_of_icc_get(dev, "write");
+	if (IS_ERR(write))
+		return PTR_ERR(write);
+
+	if (read) {
+		err = icc_set_bw(read, eqos_icc_avg_kbps, eqos_icc_peak_kbps);
+		if (err)
+			return err;
+	}
+
+	if (write) {
+		err = icc_set_bw(write, eqos_icc_avg_kbps, eqos_icc_peak_kbps);
+		if (err)
+			return err;
+	}
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
 static int dwc_eth_dwmac_config_dt(struct platform_device *pdev,
 				   struct plat_stmmacenet_data *plat_dat)
 {
@@ -224,6 +274,11 @@
 	if (!is_of_node(dev->fwnode))
 		goto bypass_clk_reset_gpio;
 
+	err = tegra_eqos_init_icc(dev);
+	if (err)
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, err,
+				     "failed to request interconnect bandwidth\n");
+
 	plat_dat->clk_tx_i = stmmac_pltfr_find_clk(plat_dat, "tx");
 
 	eqos->reset = devm_gpiod_get(&pdev->dev, "phy-reset", GPIOD_OUT_HIGH);
